From: Andrea Campanella <emuboy85@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mips: No sqrt builtin with single float

With -msingle-float the compiler has no sqrt.d instruction, so
__builtin_sqrt becomes a call to sqrt, and __ieee754_sqrt calls itself.
Keep the builtin for sqrtf only. The same guard exists for fma.


Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [PlayStation 2 port]
---
 sysdeps/mips/fpu/math-use-builtins-sqrt.h | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/sysdeps/mips/fpu/math-use-builtins-sqrt.h
+++ b/sysdeps/mips/fpu/math-use-builtins-sqrt.h
@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@
 #include <sgidefs.h>
 
-#define USE_SQRT_BUILTIN (_MIPS_ISA >= _MIPS_ISA_MIPS2)
+#ifdef __mips_single_float
+# define USE_SQRT_BUILTIN 0
+#else
+# define USE_SQRT_BUILTIN (_MIPS_ISA >= _MIPS_ISA_MIPS2)
+#endif
 #define USE_SQRTF_BUILTIN (_MIPS_ISA >= _MIPS_ISA_MIPS2)
 #define USE_SQRTL_BUILTIN 0
 #define USE_SQRTF128_BUILTIN 0
